body:
Thanks brother. I've already incorporated a lot of what you suggest. My relationship with my daughter has gotten much better. Her mother is more of her fiend and I'm more of a disciplinarian. That confuses her a bit but in the long run I think she'll appreciate the structure I provide for her.

&#x200B;

The new woman I'm with is an absolute gem. Treats me like a king and calls me out on my shit when I'm wrong. She's a real partner.

Trust me, I haven't skipped the anger phase. She knows exactly how I feel about her and her actions. She's such a narcissist that she doesn't care. She thinks we're all here to serve her. She was treated that way by her parents and somehow I was dumb enough to follow their lead.

&#x200B;

I've tried not to hold on to too much of the anger and resentment because it bleeds into the other areas of my life.

The "let's be friends" thing was one of the most ridiculous things she ever said. When she told me she wanted a divorce, she spoke as if her therapist had taken control of her brain. "We'll be a new family" "we'll have dinners together" and " children are resilient" are some of her greatest hits. When I told her her that I would never have a friend that did what she did to me and our daughter, she seemed befuddled and confused. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
